/* =============================================================================
 * EVO PLAYER - embedded fallback provider skin (#90 scope 14)
 *
 * The stylesheet for provider_fallback.rml. Also the worked example of the
 * RCSS subset the sceAgc backend actually implements - every property used
 * here is one docs/addons/provider-architecture.md lists as supported, and
 * nothing here relies on anything outside it. A bundle that stays inside this
 * vocabulary renders the same on the console as it does under uiview.sh.
 *
 * Provider contexts do NOT receive the theme push. evo_rmlui_set_theme stamps
 * colours onto every element as inline properties, which would silently
 * overwrite a provider's own palette, so the colours here are literal - and a
 * bundle's colours are literally its own.
 * ============================================================================= */

body {
    font-family: LatoLatin;
    font-weight: normal;
    font-size: 18dp;
    color: #e8e8ecff;
    background-color: #101014ff;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    width: 1920dp;
    height: 1080dp;
    overflow: hidden;
}

div, span, p, img {
    box-sizing: border-box;
}

#pf-root {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    padding-top: 48dp;
    padding-bottom: 48dp;
    /*
     * 152dp of that left inset is EVO's navigation rail.
     *
     * The rail is a document in EVO's MAIN context and is composited over a
     * provider context afterwards (ProviderHostScreen::render), so it is not
     * in this document's layout and nothing here reserves room for it
     * automatically. At the old 96dp this skin drew its title, its error bar
     * and its first column of initials underneath the rail - invisible in the
     * host preview until the preview started compositing the rail too, and
     * never noticed on hardware because the screen it happens on is the one
     * nobody wants to be looking at.
     *
     * Every bundle owes the same gutter; it is in the vocabulary section of
     * docs/addons/provider-architecture.md for that reason.
     */
    padding-left: 200dp;
    padding-right: 64dp;
}

/* ---- header ------------------------------------------------------------ */

/*
 * display: block is spelled out on every element that needs it.
 *
 * RmlUi's `display` property DEFAULTS TO INLINE, for a div as much as for a
 * span - it has no HTML default stylesheet behind it. Leaving it out laid the
 * title, the breadcrumb and the error chip on one line and dropped #pf-root's
 * padding entirely, so the whole document sat flush against the screen edge.
 * This is the single most common way a bundle written like HTML goes wrong.
 */
#pf-header {
    display: block;
    height: 100dp;
}

#pf-title {
    display: block;
    font-family: LatoLatin;
    font-weight: bold;
    font-size: 40dp;
    color: #ffffffff;
}

#pf-crumb {
    display: block;
    font-size: 17dp;
    color: #8a8a96ff;
    margin-top: 6dp;
}

/* ---- status ------------------------------------------------------------ */
/*
 * A bundle that fails to load must say so. The error state is a visible red
 * bar, not a log line: on a console the log is not reachable while the screen
 * is up, so an unexplained fallback skin is indistinguishable from a bug in
 * the provider itself.
 */
#pf-status {
    display: block;
    padding: 12dp 18dp;
    margin-bottom: 20dp;
    border-radius: 6dp;
    font-size: 17dp;
    background-color: #1c2a1cff;
    color: #9fd89fff;
}

#pf-status.pf-err {
    background-color: #341a1aff;
    color: #ff9e9eff;
}

#pf-loading,
#pf-empty {
    display: block;
    padding: 24dp 0;
    font-size: 19dp;
    color: #8a8a96ff;
}

/* ---- rows -------------------------------------------------------------- */

#pf-list {
    display: block;
    height: 700dp;
    overflow-y: auto;
}

.pf-row {
    /*
     * nav: auto is what makes the D-pad work. RmlUi's spatial navigation reads
     * these properties to decide where focus goes next; with the default
     * `none` the context receives the key press and does nothing, which looks
     * exactly like a hung screen.
     */
    /* Focusable. RmlUi has no `tabindex` attribute - focusability is this
     * RCSS property, and without it the row is skipped by both Tab and the
     * D-pad. */
    tab-index: auto;
    nav: auto;
    display: block;
    height: 92dp;
    padding: 10dp 16dp;
    margin-bottom: 8dp;
    border-radius: 8dp;
    background-color: #17171dff;
}

/* The focus ring is the provider's to draw. EVO pushes no is_focused bool and
 * has no idea which row this is. */
.pf-row:focus {
    background-color: #24242eff;
    border: 2dp #6ea8feff;
}

.pf-art {
    display: inline-block;
    width: 72dp;
    height: 72dp;
    border-radius: 6dp;
    /* Something behind the gap while the poster is still downloading. A
     * provider's art arrives over several frames, so a row with no background
     * flashes empty on every navigation. */
    background-color: #202028ff;
    vertical-align: top;
}

.pf-art img {
    width: 72dp;
    height: 72dp;
    border-radius: 6dp;
}

/* The title's first letter, when a row has no artwork. `row.initial` is
 * published by the host because RmlUi has no substring transform. */
.pf-initial {
    font-family: LatoLatin;
    font-weight: bold;
    font-size: 32dp;
    color: #4a4a58ff;
    text-align: center;
    padding-top: 16dp;
}

.pf-text {
    display: inline-block;
    /* 1656dp of content width, less the art column (72 + 20 of padding) and
     * the right-hand meta column (200). */
    width: 1330dp;
    padding-left: 20dp;
    vertical-align: top;
}

.pf-row-title {
    display: block;
    font-weight: bold;
    font-size: 21dp;
    color: #ffffffff;
    white-space: nowrap;
    overflow: hidden;
}

.pf-row-sub,
.pf-row-now {
    display: block;
    font-size: 16dp;
    color: #8a8a96ff;
    margin-top: 4dp;
    white-space: nowrap;
    overflow: hidden;
}

.pf-row-now {
    color: #9fb8d8ff;
}

.pf-meta {
    display: inline-block;
    width: 200dp;
    text-align: right;
    vertical-align: top;
    padding-top: 22dp;
}

.pf-badge {
    font-size: 14dp;
    font-weight: bold;
    color: #ffffffff;
    background-color: #b03434ff;
    padding: 3dp 8dp;
    border-radius: 4dp;
}

.pf-dur {
    font-size: 16dp;
    color: #8a8a96ff;
}

.pf-chev {
    font-size: 22dp;
    color: #6a6a76ff;
}

/* ---- footer ------------------------------------------------------------ */

#pf-footer {
    display: block;
    padding-top: 16dp;
    font-size: 15dp;
    color: #6a6a76ff;
}
